From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: mahua-hp-omnibook-5-bf1xxx: Update to
 Rahul Pon's current tree

Take Rahul Pon's daily device tree for the HP OmniBook 5 16-bf1xxx at
a2e04f161 (his kernel -23), in place of the 6 November copy. It adds
the sound card on the ADSP with the two WSA8845 speakers and the VA
macro's microphones, the SMB2370 eUSB2 repeaters on both USB-C ports
with the PMH0101 regulators they share, and thermal zones for four of
the embedded controller's thermistors. HP's USB-A PHY tuning is only in
his test tree, so it isn't here.

As before, the APSS CoreSight overrides go, since Linux 7.3 has no
CoreSight path on Mahua, and the GPU stays off until the kernel
supports the Adreno X2-85.

Link: https://github.com/theflyingrahul/linux-hp-omnibook-5-glymur/tree/a2e04f161/dts/qcom
Signed-off-by: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
---
-- 
2.47.0
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/mahua-hp-omnibook-5-bf1xxx.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/mahua-hp-omnibook-5-bf1xxx.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/mahua-hp-omnibook-5-bf1xxx.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/mahua-hp-omnibook-5-bf1xxx.dts
